# A triangular lamp. THIS SCENE DOES NOT LOAD YET.
#
#   image_stats: an emissive material sits on a `mesh`, which cannot hand out points of itself:
#   it would be seen and would light nothing
#
# `TriangleMesh` does not implement `AreaSampleable`, so `SceneBuilderVisitor` refuses the
# description rather than render a lamp that lights nothing. The file is here because it is the
# witness the work that lifts that restriction will be measured on. See `ideas/area_light.md` §7.
#
#   --integrator naive|path --renderer mt --threads 8 --seed 0
#   --samples_ppx 1024 --max_depth 4 --output_width 256 --output_height 192
#
# WHY IT IS A MESH AND NOT A `triangle`
#
# **The language has no triangle.** Its shapes are `sphere`, `rectangle`, `plane`, `cylinder`,
# `aabox`, `mesh` and the csg operations; a triangle exists only inside a mesh. So the lamp here is
# `test_files/lamp_triangle.ply`, three vertices and one face written by hand, and adding a
# `triangle` production instead would mean crossing lexer, parser, ast, both visitors and the
# editor support — a subject of its own, not a step of this one.
#
# WHAT IT WILL ISOLATE
#
# One triangle, so it measures the per-triangle draw and nothing else. The mesh of *several*
# triangles is a second question and wants a second witness: choosing which triangle to draw from,
# in proportion to its area, needs a cumulative sum that a single-triangle lamp never exercises.
# That witness should hold triangles of markedly unequal area, since an equal-area mesh cannot tell
# a correct choice from a uniform one.
#
# The lamp spans roughly 4 by 3.5 and hangs at the height of the panel of `direct_lighting.stage`,
# whose camera this keeps, so the two can be read against each other.

camera pin_hole
  pos 0.0 2.9 0.0
  look 0.0 0.0 0.0
  up 0.0 0.0 -1.0

scene

  object simple
    rectangle 12 12
    lambertian color 0.6 0.6 0.6

  # The lamp. The winding of the ply already aims its normal at -Y, so there is no half turn here
  # as there is on a `rectangle` lamp — see the comments in the ply itself.
  object transformed
    object simple
      mesh file "test_files/lamp_triangle.ply"
      diffuse_light color 6.0 6.0 6.0
    transform {
      translate 0.0 3.0 0.0
    }
